  "notes": "The extended-R&B voicing is the parameter: the research says m7, m9 and sus, genuine 4-bar progressions rather than vamps, and frequent modal borrowing on the bridge. So `extensions` is the most seventh/ninth-weighted in this batch (triads down to 0.15), `susSubstitutionProb` is 0.3, `borrowed` carries a dorian IV as well as V, and `harmonicRhythm` drops `vamp` entirely — the only entry here that does. The vocal row — long sustained notes, falsetto leaps, low syllable density but high melodic content — is a low `densityPerBar` over an arch-weighted contour with a raised `octaveJumpProb`, which is an unusual pairing and is what makes this melody unlike the dense ones on either side of it. ⚠ The \"heavy reverb/room on the claps so the kit reads atmospheric rather than punchy\" is authored as a wide `layerClapOffsetMs` [6, 14] plus a deeper `detuneSemis`: the model has no reverb parameter, and a late, detuned clap layer is the nearest honest thing a MIDI generator can do to it. Say so before believing the number. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium. ⚠ The slower 90–110 straight-feel subset is NOT authored — `session.halfTime` is a single flag and splitting it would need a mode; the authored band is the half-time one the research puts first. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
